---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How I Helped Build the Team and Infrastructure That Brought Barstool Sports to Tampa Bay"
  description="How Pete Guzzo helped design, staff and operate Shear Media Studios — and landed Barstool Sports, Rhonda Shear's Up All Night, 30+ podcast clients and national broadcast productions in the first nine months."
  image="/images/studios/Shear-Media-Studios-Control-Room.jpg"
>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="cs-hero">
    <div class="cs-hero-inner">
      <a href="/work" class="cs-back">← Back to Work</a>
      <p class="cs-eyebrow">Strategy · Studio Operations · Business Development</p>
      <h1 class="cs-h1">How I Helped Build the Team and Infrastructure That Brought Barstool Sports — and Other Clients — to Tampa Bay</h1>
      <p class="cs-hero-sub">Strategy first. We build what the market needs. We put the right team around it. Then we go sell it.</p>
      <div class="cs-hero-meta">
        <div class="cs-meta-item"><span class="cs-meta-label">Role</span><span class="cs-meta-val">EVP — Strategy, Studio Operations & Business Development</span></div>
        <div class="cs-meta-item"><span class="cs-meta-label">Facility</span><span class="cs-meta-val">Shear Media Studios · St. Petersburg, FL</span></div>
        <div class="cs-meta-item"><span class="cs-meta-label">Scope</span><span class="cs-meta-val">Strategy, infrastructure, team, operations, client development</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-hero-globe">
      <img src="/images/studios/SMS-SRT-Transmission-Globe.png" alt="Broadcast transmission from Tampa Bay to control rooms across the US, UK, Canada, and Australia" class="cs-globe-img" loading="eager" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROOF STRIP -->
  <section class="cs-proof">
    <div class="cs-proof-inner">
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">20</span><span class="cs-stat-label">Control room inputs</span></div>
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">2</span><span class="cs-stat-label">VFX channels</span></div>
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">0</span><span class="cs-stat-label">Missed live broadcasts</span></div>
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">4</span><span class="cs-stat-label">Countries working with / broadcasting into</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE CAPABILITY -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-light">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">The capability</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">When a client asks, "Can we do this?" I want our answer to be yes.</h2>
      <div class="cs-body-wide">
        <p class="cs-body">When I started developing the strategy for Shear Media Studios, I saw an opportunity to build something Tampa Bay needed: one connected production facility capable of serving everything from podcasters and content creators to commercials, films, live productions and national broadcast clients.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">That meant thinking beyond individual rooms.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">A roughly 15,000-square-foot facility with multiple studios patched together through their own mixers and switchers and connected through a central control room.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-cap-grid">
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Live Streaming</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Fully Capable Control Room</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Transmission to Remote Control Rooms — SRT + Broadcast Contribution</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Multiple Lighting Grids + Lighting Control</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Multiple Studios + Sets, Independent or Together</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Podcast + Creator Environments</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="cs-cap-close">The goal was pretty simple: when a client asks, "Can we do this?" I want our answer to be yes. And then we figure out the best way to do it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BUILD THE CAPABILITY FOR THE CLIENT -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">Build the capability for the client</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">I don't believe in "build it and they will come."</h2>
      <div class="cs-body-wide">
        <p class="cs-body">You have to understand what people are going to need, design for it, build the team and then go sell it.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">So that's what we did.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">I worked with Rhonda Shear, Van Fagan and an incredible mix of studio managers, production people, engineers, technicians, crew and partners to keep turning Shear Media Studios into one connected production operation.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">The building itself became part of the strategy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-pillars">
        <div class="cs-pillar">
          <h3 class="cs-pillar-title">Studio G. Studio A.</h3>
          <p class="cs-pillar-body">Podcast environments. Multiple sets. Control. Audio. Lighting. Transmission. Connected where they need to be.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-pillar">
          <h3 class="cs-pillar-title">Independent where they need to be.</h3>
          <p class="cs-pillar-body">Each space can run its own production. The control room connects all of them when the job calls for it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-pillar">
          <h3 class="cs-pillar-title">Flexible for every client.</h3>
          <p class="cs-pillar-body">Not designing the entire business around one type of client. That's what makes it work for all of them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LIVE STREAMING, SRT + BROADCAST -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-light">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">Live streaming, SRT + broadcast</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">Your talent can be in Tampa while your production team is somewhere else.</h2>
      <div class="cs-body-wide">
        <p class="cs-body">Shear Media Studios can live stream directly to platforms <strong>and</strong> transmit professional camera signals to another control room for remote production.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">That's really all the client needs to know.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">Your cameras can originate here while another control room handles the production. Your executives can watch remotely. Your talent stays in Tampa.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">Years before COVID, Gene May and I were already experimenting with giving remote clients the actual camera feed — not a behind-the-scenes view — so they could participate in a production without physically being on set.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">I carried that thinking into Shear.</p>
      </div>
      <blockquote class="cs-pull-quote">
        If we're going to have a control room, it should be able to talk to other control rooms.
      </blockquote>
      <p class="cs-body cs-body-wide">SRT and broadcast transmission became part of the plan before we knew exactly which client would need it. Then one did.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- AND THEN BARSTOOL SHOWED UP -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">And then Barstool showed up</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">Within our first nine months, I got the opportunity to bid on a recurring Barstool Sports professional football production.</h2>
      <div class="cs-two-col cs-barstool-cols">
        <div>
          <p class="cs-body">Custom set in Studio G. Six cameras. Weekly live production. Remote control room.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">Suddenly infrastructure we'd been planning "just in case" had exactly the client we'd been building it for.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">So I sold it. Then we had to make the damn thing work.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">During the first transmission test, we hit a network problem involving routing, port forwarding and SRT. Five engineers were waiting for us to connect.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <blockquote class="cs-pull-quote-light">
            I'm not a network engineer. I'm the guy who helped sell the production and needed the network to work.
          </blockquote>
          <p class="cs-body">Fortunately, I'd spent months on nights and weekends building AI agents and CORTEX specifically to help me attack problems I didn't already know how to solve.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">I paired those tools with Codex, dug through our network documentation with the team, worked through the routing and transmission path, and learned what I needed in real time.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">Signals connected. Test cleared. Show live.</p>
          <p class="cs-body cs-missed-zero"><strong>And we've never missed one.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- NINE MONTHS. A LOT MORE THAN ONE CLIENT. -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-light">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">Nine months. A lot more than one client.</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">Barstool is a great win. But it's one piece of what we've built.</h2>
      <div class="cs-result-grid">
        <div class="cs-result-block cs-result-block-light">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title-light">Rhonda Shear — Up All Night</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">The name on the building deserves a little love. Rhonda Shear's Up All Night brings original entertainment production into the facility — building on Rhonda's television legacy while creating something new from inside Shear Media Studios. Now on Roku.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-block cs-result-block-light">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title-light">Barstool Sports</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Recurring national professional football production. Custom Studio G set. Six-camera workflow. Remote broadcast production and transmission.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-block cs-result-block-light">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title-light">30+ Podcast Clients + Creators</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Creators, businesses and personalities using multiple configurations throughout the facility — from simple conversations to larger produced shows.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-block cs-result-block-light">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title-light">Commercials + Branded Content</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Major commercial and branded productions using the facility, crews, stages, equipment and connected production infrastructure.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-block cs-result-block-light">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title-light">Film + Specialty Series</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Film, episodic and specialty productions that need more than a room — they need a production home.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE INFRASTRUCTURE KEEPS MOVING -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark">
    <div class="cs-container cs-two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">The infrastructure keeps moving</p>
        <h2 class="cs-h2">That's probably the part I like most. We're not done.</h2>
        <p class="cs-body">We're developing multiple-set configurations in Studio A. Expanding podcast access. Finding new ways to use the control room and connected infrastructure.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">Watching how clients, crews and creators actually use the building and designing around them.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">Because you don't really finish a production studio when construction ends.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="cs-connected-list cs-connected-list-dark">
        <li>Multiple studios + sets</li>
        <li>Multiple lighting grids</li>
        <li>Individual mixers and switchers</li>
        <li>Central control room</li>
        <li>Podcast + creator environments</li>
        <li>Live streaming</li>
        <li>SRT + broadcast transmission</li>
        <li class="cs-connected-last-dark">The people using it help you finish it.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE PRINCIPLE -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark cs-strategy-section">
    <div class="cs-container cs-strategy-inner">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">The principle</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2 cs-strategy-h2">I didn't help design Shear Media Studios for Barstool Sports. I helped design an operation where a Barstool Sports could happen.</h2>
      <p class="cs-body">And a Rhonda Shear show. And a podcast. And a commercial. And a film. And whatever walks through the door next.</p>
      <p class="cs-body">That's the strategy.</p>
      <div class="cs-strategy-lines">
        <div class="cs-strategy-line">See what the market needs.</div>
        <div class="cs-strategy-line">Build the capability.</div>
        <div class="cs-strategy-line">Build the team.</div>
        <div class="cs-strategy-line">Sell it.</div>
        <div class="cs-strategy-line cs-strategy-last">Then keep making it better.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark cs-cta-section">
    <div class="cs-container cs-cta-inner">
      <h2 class="cs-cta-head">Need someone who can think like this and build like this?</h2>
      <p class="cs-cta-sub">Strategy, infrastructure, operations, client development — or all four. Let's talk.</p>
      <div class="cs-cta-btns">
        <a href="/contact" class="cs-btn-primary">Talk to Pete →</a>
        <a href="https://www.shearmediastudios.com/live-transmission" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cs-btn-secondary">See Shear Media Studios →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ─── TOKENS ─── */
  :root {
    --cs-ink: #1c1917;
    --cs-paper: #f5f0eb;
    --cs-rust: #9b4a2a;
    --cs-dark-bg: #0d0f14;
    --cs-dark-surface: #151820;
    --cs-dark-border: rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
    --cs-dark-text: #e8e2da;
    --cs-dark-muted: rgba(232,226,218,0.60);
    --cs-accent: #5ea8e6;
    --cs-accent-warm: #f1f6a4;
    --cs-container: 72rem;
    --cs-px: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  /* ─── HERO ─── */
  .cs-hero {
    background: var(--cs-dark-bg);
    color: var(--cs-dark-text);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    max-width: var(--cs-container);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem var(--cs-px) 5rem;
  }
  .cs-back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--cs-dark-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }
  .cs-back:hover { color: var(--cs-dark-text); }
  .cs-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--cs-accent-warm);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .cs-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.2vw, 2.75rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: #fff;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .cs-hero-sub {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--cs-accent-warm);
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .cs-hero-meta { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .cs-meta-item { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .cs-meta-label { color: var(--cs-accent); font-weight: 600; min-width: 4rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 0.7rem; padding-top: 0.05rem; }
  .cs-meta-val { color: var(--cs-dark-muted); }
  .cs-hero-globe { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  .cs-globe-img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 480px;
    mix-blend-mode: lighten;
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, #000 58%, transparent 72%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, #000 58%, transparent 72%);
  }

  /* ─── PROOF STRIP ─── */
  .cs-proof {
    background: var(--cs-dark-surface);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border);
  }
  .cs-proof-inner {
    max-width: var(--cs-container);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem var(--cs-px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem 1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .cs-proof-stat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; }
  .cs-stat-num { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 3rem); color: #fff; line-height: 1.15; }
  .cs-stat-label { font-size: 0.7rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--cs-accent-warm); text-wrap: balance; }

  /* ─── SECTIONS ─── */
  .cs-section { padding: 5rem 0; }
  .cs-light { background: var(--cs-paper); color: var(--cs-ink); }
  .cs-dark { background: var(--cs-dark-bg); color: var(--cs-dark-text); }
  .cs-container { max-width: var(--cs-container); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--cs-px); }
  .cs-section-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .cs-light .cs-section-eyebrow { color: var(--cs-rust); }
  .cs-dark .cs-section-eyebrow { color: var(--cs-accent-warm); }
  .cs-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.8vw, 2.25rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
  .cs-light .cs-h2 { color: var(--cs-ink); }
  .cs-dark .cs-h2 { color: #fff; }
  .cs-body { font-size: 0.975rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .cs-light .cs-body { color: rgba(28,25,23,0.75); }
  .cs-dark .cs-body { color: var(--cs-dark-muted); }
  .cs-body-wide { max-width: 46rem; }

  /* ─── TWO-COL ─── */
  .cs-two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4rem; align-items: center; }
  .cs-img-block { border-radius: 0.5rem; overflow: hidden; }
  .cs-img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }

  /* ─── PILLARS ─── */
  .cs-pillars { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 2rem; margin-top: 3rem; }
  .cs-pillar { border-top: 2px solid var(--cs-dark-border); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  .cs-pillar-n { font-size: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--cs-accent); font-weight: 700; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .cs-pillar-title { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: 1.05rem; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .cs-pillar-body { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--cs-dark-muted); }

  /* ─── RESULT GRID ─── */
  .cs-result-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .cs-result-block { border-top: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  .cs-result-title { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--cs-accent-warm); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
  .cs-result-block-light { border-top-color: rgba(28,25,23,0.12); }
  .cs-result-title-light { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--cs-rust); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }

  /* ─── CTA ─── */
  .cs-cta-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border); }
  .cs-cta-inner { text-align: center; padding: 5rem var(--cs-px); max-width: var(--cs-container); margin: 0 auto; }
  .cs-cta-head { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.8vw, 2.5rem); color: #fff; margin: 0 0 1rem; max-width: 36rem; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .cs-cta-sub { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--cs-dark-muted); max-width: 32rem; margin: 0 auto 2.5rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .cs-cta-btns { display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .cs-btn-primary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 0.875rem 2rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; background: var(--cs-paper); color: var(--cs-ink); text-decoration: none; transition: background 0.2s; letter-spacing: 0.02em; }
  .cs-btn-primary:hover { background: #fff; }
  .cs-btn-secondary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 0.875rem 2rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; border: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border); color: var(--cs-dark-text); text-decoration: none; transition: border-color 0.2s; }
  .cs-btn-secondary:hover { border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); }

  /* ─── CAPABILITY GRID ─── */
  .cs-cap-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.12);
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
  .cs-cap-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 1.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.08);
    border-right: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.08);
  }
  .cs-cap-item:nth-child(3n) { border-right: none; padding-right: 0; }
  .cs-cap-name {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: rgba(28,25,23,0.45);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .cs-cap-yes {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    color: var(--cs-rust);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .cs-cap-close {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: rgba(28,25,23,0.5);
    font-style: italic;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  /* ─── MANTRA ─── */
  .cs-mantra {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    align-self: center;
  }
  .cs-mantra-line {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2.2rem);
    color: var(--cs-ink);
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .cs-mantra-then {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: rgba(28,25,23,0.45);
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* ─── PULL QUOTES ─── */
  .cs-pull-quote {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.2vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--cs-accent);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--cs-accent);
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1.5rem;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
  .cs-pull-quote-light {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.7vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--cs-rust);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--cs-rust);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

